# Implementation Plan — Convex Cron Jobs, Auto-Caching, Stale Data Purging & AI Predictor Synchronization

Thorough audit and resolution plan to ensure Convex cron jobs are registered, active, and automatically purging stale cache data while populating the database with fixtures, odds, stats, AI multi-agent analysis, and verdicts across all 6 sports (Football, Basketball, Tennis, Rally, Ice Hockey, Baseball) so the AI Predictor UI is fully populated and synchronized.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Environment Variables on Convex Backend**: The AI Predictor relies on server-side Convex actions to fetch odds/fixtures and run LLM analyses via `Agnes AI` and `OpenRouter`. We will push all required environment variables (`AGNES_AI_KEY`, `JINA_API_KEY`, `FIRECRAWL_API_KEY`, `SERPER_API_KEY`, `BRIGHTDATA_API_KEY`, `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, `PREDICTOR_DAILY_CAP`) into the Convex deployment (`modest-lark-218`) via `npx convex env set` and deploy the updated Convex functions and cron definitions via `npx convex deploy`.

> [!TIP]
> **Cascading Stale Data Purge**: To prevent database bloating and ensure fresh projections, the daily purge job (`predictor-purge-daily`) will be upgraded to perform a full cascading delete across all Convex tables (`predictorDays`, `predictorMatches`, `predictorVerdicts`, and `aiPredictorStats`) for records older than 7 days before starting a new daily cache cycle.

